---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Signup from '../../components/Signup.astro';
import { utilities, smallUtilities, countiesFor, ptcAsOf } from '../../data/utilities';
const rows = utilities.map((u) => ({ ...u, counties: countiesFor(u.code).main }));
---
<Base
  title="Pennsylvania electric utilities and community solar"
  description="Community solar guides for PECO, PPL, Duquesne Light, Met-Ed, Penelec, Penn Power, and West Penn Power customers, with each utility's price to compare and service area."
>
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Utility guides</div>
      <h1>Community solar, utility by utility</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        In Pennsylvania, community solar runs through your electric utility. Your utility decides
        which projects you could join and is where your bill credits would show up. Find yours below.
      </p>
      <p><a class="btn" href="/zip-lookup">Find my utility by ZIP code</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Utility</th><th>Main counties</th><th>Price to compare*</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {rows.map((u) => (
              <tr>
                <td><a href={`/utilities/${u.slug}`}><strong>{u.name}</strong></a><br /><span class="muted">{u.parent}</span></td>
                <td>{u.counties.join(', ')}</td>
                <td class="num">{u.ptc.toFixed(2)}¢</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="updated">*Residential price to compare in cents per kWh, as of {ptcAsOf}. Prices change from time to time, usually at least twice a year. Check current prices at <a href="https://www.papowerswitch.com/" rel="noopener">PA PowerSwitch</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="other">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Smaller utilities</h2>
      <p>A few smaller regulated utilities serve parts of the state. As Pennsylvania-regulated electric utilities, their customers would likely be covered by the community solar bill too.</p>
      <ul>
        {smallUtilities.map((s) => <li><strong>{s.name}</strong>: {s.area}</li>)}
      </ul>

      <h2>Electric co-ops and borough utilities</h2>
      <p>
        Many rural Pennsylvanians get power from an electric cooperative, and some towns run their
        own borough electric systems. HB 504 works through the state's regulated electric
        distribution companies, so as written it likely would not apply to co-op or borough
        customers. We'll update this page as the bill and program rules take shape.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Signup />
</Base>

<style>
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
  th { font-size: .8rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--muted); background: var(--green-100); }
  td.num { white-space: nowrap; font-weight: 700; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { th, td { padding: 10px; font-size: .95rem; } }
</style>
